    <div class="workflow-title">Observable Feeding Pattern</div>
    <ol class="workflow-steps">
      <li><div><strong>Operation Concludes</strong>Named operation ends. Arrest count released. Press conference held. Public attention disperses. The machine enters its inter-operation phase. The Ledger continues updating.<span class="doctrine-tag">[Doctrine: No documented off-switch]</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>Hotlist Persistence</strong>ALPR alert profiles remain active on all vehicles associated with the operation. Plates tagged during pre-seizure analysis continue generating hits on every <span class="rx" data-len="──────────">&nbsp;</span> camera in the network. The operation never fully ends for the vehicles it flagged.<span class="doctrine-tag">[Doctrine: Flock Safety Data Retention Policy]</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>Quarterly Inspection Rotation</strong><span class="rx" data-len="────">&nbsp;</span> Group Supervisors and Special Agents perform mandatory drive-by physical inspection of each real property in the pre-seizure queue within their Area of Responsibility. Condition verified. Photographs taken. File updated. The <span class="rx" data-len="────">&nbsp;</span> handbook requires this on a quarterly schedule regardless of operational tempo.<span class="doctrine-tag">[Doctrine: HSI AIRG Handbook §4.5]</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>Pre-Seizure File Maintenance</strong>Title search updated when deed activity is recorded. Appraisal refreshed when comparable sales occur. Net equity recalculated when land values move. The file that preceded the last operation is maintained in preparation for the next one. The property owner does not know the file exists.<span class="doctrine-tag">[Doctrine: HSI AIRG Handbook — Pre-Seizure Analysis Requirements]</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>Claim Boundary Maintenance</strong><span class="rx" data-len="───────">&nbsp;</span> and <span class="rx" data-len="───">&nbsp;</span> pipelines maintain their respective claim assignments from the previous operation. Properties assigned to each fund in pre-seizure analysis retain that assignment. Inter-agency deference protocol holds. The harvest has already been divided.<span class="doctrine-tag">[Doctrine: 28 USC §524(c) · 31 USC §9703 · Equitable Sharing]</span></div></li>
      <li><div><strong>Fiscal Calendar Alignment</strong>Summer operations preferred. September 30 fiscal year close drives operational tempo. Properties scoring highest on the updated Ledger move to the top of the harvest queue as the calendar rotates toward the next named operation window.<span class="doctrine-tag">[Doctrine: TFF No-Year Budget Authority · Annual Performance Target — 95% High-Impact]</span></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <div class="margin-col">
    <div class="doctrine-entry">
      <div class="doctrine-label">Primary Source · Witness Account</div>
      <div class="doctrine-name">The Black SUV — <span class="rx" data-len="─────────────────">&nbsp;</span>, AR</div>
      <div class="doctrine-stated">Observed: Black SUV, male driver, female passenger photographing a lake-view property from a moving vehicle at approximately 3 mph. One week later: <span class="rx" data-len="────────────">&nbsp;</span>s lining the road for the arrest of one warranted individual living with his father at the same property.</div>
      <div class="doctrine-actual">Analysis: The passenger's photographic documentation is consistent with the <span class="rx" data-len="────">&nbsp;</span> handbook §4.5 quarterly condition verification requirement. The warrant provided legal access. The property provided the operational objective. The interval between observation and arrest is consistent with pre-seizure file finalization before operational execution.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="doctrine-divider"></div>
    <div class="doctrine-entry">
      <div class="doctrine-label">Enabling Doctrine</div>
      <div class="doctrine-name">The Warrant as Mechanism</div>
      <div class="doctrine-stated">Stated purpose: Warrant authorizes arrest of named individual for documented criminal conduct.</div>
      <div class="doctrine-actual">Actual operation: Warrant provides legal entry to property already identified in pre-seizure analysis. The arrest is the administrative mechanism. The property is the operational objective. The sequence — inspection, then warrant execution, then seizure — is documented in the <span class="rx" data-len="────">&nbsp;</span> handbook as the preferred order of operations.</div>
